# Google Search Console indexing (learned 2026-09-27)

**Invariant:** Public shop URLs (home, stickers hubs/subcats, products, Market S, about/contact/legal) stay crawlable with **www** canonicals. Private/account/cart/checkout stay out of robots + sitemap. Parent layouts must **not** force child routes to inherit a hub-only canonical.

## GSC buckets (owner mail ~Sep 2026)

| Reason | Likely cause in this repo |
|--------|---------------------------|
| Alternate with proper canonical (~4) | `/stickers/*` subpages inherited `canonical: /stickers` from `stickers/layout.tsx` |
| Blocked by robots.txt (~1) | Expected for `/admin` / `/api` / auth reset — expand private Disallows carefully |
| Crawled – not indexed (~2) | Thin or low-value URLs still in sitemap (cart/checkout/login) or weak subcategory SEO |

## Do

- `robots.ts`: Disallow admin/api/auth resets **and** cart/checkout/orders/profile/login/register/unsubscribe.
- `sitemap.ts`: omit those private paths; keep product + category URLs.
- Per-route `buildPublicMetadata({ path })` for sticker subcategories; hub metadata only on `/stickers` page layout segment.
- `noindex` layouts for cart/checkout/account tooling if still reachable.

## Do not

- Disallow `/stickers`, `/products`, `/hot-goods`, or `/`.
- Put apex `selpic.com.au` in canonical/sitemap (use `www` via `getPublicSiteUrl`).
